	"notes": "This is the official Python documentation home page, and it is one of the oldest, plainest layouts in this set: a navigation list on the left and the reading text on the right. The surprising part only shows up when you compare the screenshots at different sizes side by side — the paragraph of text is exactly the same width on a laptop, a desktop monitor and an ultrawide screen. It does not get wider or narrower; the page just leaves a big empty strip of white space on the right on a large screen instead of using it. Most modern sites either stretch the text or cap it and centre it in the middle; this page caps it and pins it to the left instead, which is a real (if old-fashioned) design choice. On a phone the whole left-hand navigation list disappears behind a small hamburger icon instead of moving underneath the text, which is a slightly different trick from most sidebars in this set.",
